WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.299
Yeah. I don't even know
why it's that coordinated

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.926
with all kinds of people, you know.

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:11.720
put the chain into a soup,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.680
and then it goes to a kitchen, and --

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.348
If you have the chain, you run out.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.810
Hi, my name is Octave
Durham, nickname Oky.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.645
I did more than 10,000 burglaries.

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.480
I've robbed everything you can imagine.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.481
My name is Arthur Brand.

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:24.357
I'm from the Netherlands.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.692
I'm an art detective.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.360
I'm responsible for recovering

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.863
250 million [pounds] of stolen art.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.074
We now work together in
trying to prevent art heists.

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:34.826
We are going to look at diamond heists

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:35.994
from Hollywood movies,

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:38.663
and we're go to watch
how realistic they are.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:49.257
If you do this in real life inside,

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:50.759
everybody would --

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.469
would have been dead, I guess.

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:56.681
No, but look at the mechanism as well.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.767
I mean, it doesn't look like that.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.149
I did this a couple of times,

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:08.526
and they don't open like that. No way.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:12.030
You have a door and there is a lock on it,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.073
but with two keys,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:16.785
one from the bank
employee, and one from you.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.328
But it's one piece.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:21.498
So if you cut this one out,
this one is still here.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.751
You have to pull them both
out and then lift them open.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.461
But the first time I did that,

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.630
I had blisters this thick
the first time I did it.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.048
I couldn't use my hands.

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:34.677
I underestimated how much
power I had to use to open it.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:36.304
And I opened a few hundred,

00:01:36.304 --> 00:01:38.473
so every time the screwdriver was going,

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:40.934
my palm of my hand, my
hands were this thick.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.851
It really hurt.

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:49.567
It takes at least three,
four minutes to open one.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.111
And the small ones are very tough.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.403
And the ones who were on top,

00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:53.863
because I can't put any pressure --

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:56.032
if they were on this
height, I can open it.

00:01:56.032 --> 00:01:57.492
But if they were this height,

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:01.246
I couldn't, you know, put
any strength on it or power.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:03.957
So, a good tip, if you have
a safety deposit in a bank,

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.709
make sure it's small and it's on top.

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:08.628
But what do you find in it?

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.796
Oky: Everything.
Arthur: Diamonds, gold?

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.880
Everything, everything.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.591
You'll find diamonds, gold, pearls,

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:18.179
but you'll also find very heavy pictures

00:02:18.179 --> 00:02:21.432
and stuff like that,
that you can really --

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:24.185
I'm not into that, but
what's it called? Extortion?

00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:25.019
You could extort.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:26.146
Really, we see pictures --

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:30.775
or you see people who have a completely,

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:31.818
they have a double life.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.820
I took a bag. And at that time,

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.656
I'm talking about 25 years ago --

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.200
it had only videotapes.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.743
And at that time,

00:02:40.743 --> 00:02:42.787
a videotape recorded with a little screen.

00:02:42.787 --> 00:02:44.122
So if you opened it, you could see it.

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:45.165
It's like a laptop.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.334
I think he was watching adult
movies in the safe, you know?

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.130
What? Why is it in the safe? [laughs]

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.219
Most of the time, they're
in envelopes, small ones.

00:02:58.219 --> 00:02:59.470
It looks good in the movie,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.306
but I never found them like that.

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.057
I found a lot of diamonds.

00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:05.226
Official, in books, you know?

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:07.478
What they are, with the
certificate next to it.

00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:10.106
I found books with six diamonds each in it

00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:13.276
from, let's say, half a karat to 1, 1 1/2,

00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:14.277
2, 2 1/2, 3.

00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:16.821
And I found six of these books

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:19.824
that were worth 1.5 million
Swiss francs at the time.

00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:24.829
Man, I love colored stones.

00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:27.540
Some diamonds with some special color

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.625
are very expensive.

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:30.585
But most of the time,

00:03:30.585 --> 00:03:33.588
especially the yellow ones
are just off-color diamonds.

00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:35.506
You know, they're not worth that much.

00:03:35.506 --> 00:03:37.467
Most of the time they're cheaper,

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.219
unless they are flawless.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.054
Most of these gangs, they know people

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.473
who can sell this stuff. You know?

00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:45.558
They can say, "This is good. This is not."

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.392
And they will sell it.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.603
If they make you do a job like this

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:51.231
and they know you don't
know nothing about value,

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.565
you get screwed, of course.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.608
Arthur: They rip you off.

00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:54.734
Oky: That's the diamond business, anyway.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.527
That's it. [laughs]

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:58.738
That's ridiculous. I
don't want to rate it.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.572
No.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.157
It doesn't get a rate.

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:06.704
This is a clip

00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:11.292
about one of the most famous
heists ever, in England.

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:14.504
In 2015, a bunch of senior guys

00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:17.548
decided to rob a safety-deposit store

00:04:17.548 --> 00:04:20.093
somewhere in Hatton Garden, in London.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:22.512
They got away with diamonds and gold

00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:24.347
worth hundreds of millions.

00:04:24.347 --> 00:04:25.515
Finally, they got caught,

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:27.934
but still a big part of the loot is gone.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.354
Kenny: Are you there?

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:32.188
Can you hear me?

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:33.314
XXX: Yeah, we can hear you.

00:04:33.314 --> 00:04:35.984
There's someone at the front door.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.448
In this scene, the alarm goes off

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.493
and the guard doesn't take action.

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:46.494
This does happen.

00:04:46.494 --> 00:04:48.204
Just a few months ago,

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:49.497
I was involved in cracking

00:04:49.497 --> 00:04:52.375
one of the biggest art
heists ever in Europe.

00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:53.710
In 2012,

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.588
a guy entered the
National Gallery in Athens

00:04:57.588 --> 00:04:59.215
and stole a Picasso.

00:04:59.215 --> 00:05:04.012
He set off the alarm on
purpose more than 100 times.

00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:06.264
So every time, the guard came looking,

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:07.932
watching for an intruder,

00:05:07.932 --> 00:05:11.519
but he was standing behind the curtains.

00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:13.313
So after a while, the guy thought,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.981
"There is some technical failure."

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.983
So he stopped showing up.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.192
And at that moment,

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:20.945
the guy had a few minutes
to steal the Picasso.

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:23.531
And don't forget, 95%,

00:05:23.531 --> 00:05:25.033
in the Netherlands,

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:29.495
of the alarms are fake.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:32.874
Yeah, when an alarm goes
off, in so many cases,

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:36.127
it's fake because there
is a bird or a curtain.

00:05:38.796 --> 00:05:39.630
Oh!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.757
[horn honks]

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:41.591
Jesus.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.053
I don't like lookout.

00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:47.638
Because if you have a lookout,

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:50.099
if you're inside, you're safe.

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:51.893
And the lookout is the one who's hot,

00:05:51.893 --> 00:05:53.811
because if he walks around,

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:55.605
people go, "Who is this
guy walking around?"

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:56.981
Can you imagine doing that?

00:05:56.981 --> 00:05:58.900
They've been in for,
what? 24 hours or longer.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.109
Just one day.
Arthur: Yeah.

00:06:00.109 --> 00:06:03.029
If they were in longer,
oof, it would've been big.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:03.863
But in this case,

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:04.989
this guy who was on the lookout

00:06:04.989 --> 00:06:06.491
even fell asleep, you know?

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:07.700
Yeah. But he's hot.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.035
You know? What are you doing here?

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.204
It's common for amateurs.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.831
But the mistake in these robberies

00:06:13.831 --> 00:06:16.501
was they were texting each other

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:17.960
with their own phones.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.880
They thought they were smart
because there's no phone tap.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.298
But now everybody knows about this.

00:06:22.298 --> 00:06:23.758
"Oh, you never call" and this and that.

00:06:23.758 --> 00:06:24.592
You don't do that.

00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:26.386
But I would rate this movie a 10,

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.054
because it shows how it went.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.807
This is one of the biggest heists ever.

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:34.727
[gags]

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:41.526
It looks like it's worth maybe

00:06:41.526 --> 00:06:43.277
$30, $40 million or something.

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:45.905
Breathe. Breathe.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:48.116
[vomiting]

00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:49.700
I don't want to take it from the person.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.620
I can see something that
the person is wearing

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.122
and then figure out where he lives,

00:06:54.122 --> 00:06:55.581
but not ever touch anybody.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.791
But most of these chains

00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:59.210
don't even have a lock to
open or close, you know?

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:03.256
And if they have, they have
maybe a triple security,

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.465
it doesn't go off in "click," one.

00:07:04.465 --> 00:07:06.843
It has to "one, two,
three," and then comes off.

00:07:06.843 --> 00:07:08.845
Most of these chains,
they go over your head,

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:10.763
if they're with these kinds of stones.

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:14.016
Why do you need a lock
to open or close it?

00:07:14.016 --> 00:07:15.518
I think this one is very heavy.

00:07:15.518 --> 00:07:16.686
It's possible to do this.

00:07:16.686 --> 00:07:19.021
You know, you have pickpocket
people who can do this.

00:07:19.021 --> 00:07:20.690
They take your watch off.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.275
You don't even notice the chain.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.317
Excuse me, we need to go --

00:07:23.317 --> 00:07:25.361
Nein! Damentoilette.

00:07:25.361 --> 00:07:27.613
The private security, they will go in.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:28.906
Nobody will stop them,

00:07:28.906 --> 00:07:31.200
because they'll have to
be with their subjects.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.702
She can't go out of sight.

00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:35.413
It's impossible that somebody
will stop these two guys.

00:07:35.413 --> 00:07:36.789
In the Netherlands, it's not allowed

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.458
